{{!
    @template local_coursedynamicrules/notification_placeholders

    The list of markers a message or prompt may contain, with a copy-to-clipboard control each.

    Both action forms render this template, and each passes the markers ITS OWN action substitutes -
    the notification action replaces {$a->courselink} with an HTML anchor, the AI action replaces
    {$a->courseurl} with a bare URL. The list used to be written here, so one of the two forms always
    advertised a marker its action did not know, and the teacher who copied it got the literal text.

    The label arrives already translated: Mustache cannot resolve a string helper whose key is held
    in a variable, so the caller looks it up. NOTE - a Mustache comment ends at the first closing
    double brace, so no example here may ever be written with the braces a real tag carries.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * markers - array, one entry per marker offered, in the order to display them
        * name - string, the marker's name without the {$a->...} wrapper
        * label - string, its translated description

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * data-action="copytoclipboard" - core/copy_to_clipboard, per marker
    * data-clipboard-target - id of the code element holding the marker text

    Example context (json):
    {
        "markers": [
            { "name": "coursename", "label": "Course name" },
            { "name": "courseurl", "label": "Course URL" }
        ]
    }
}}
<div>
    <strong>{{#str}}availableplaceholders, local_coursedynamicrules{{/str}}:</strong>
    <ul>
        {{#markers}}
        <li>
            <code id="placeholder-{{name}}">{$a->{{name}}}</code> - {{label}}
            <span class="local_coursedynamicrules_clipboard_icon" role="button"
                  data-action="copytoclipboard"
                  data-clipboard-target="#placeholder-{{name}}"
                  data-clipboard-success-message="{{#str}}copiedtoclipboard, local_coursedynamicrules{{/str}}"
                  title="{{#str}}copytoclipboard, local_coursedynamicrules{{/str}}">
                {{#pix}}t/clipboard, core{{/pix}}
            </span>
        </li>
        {{/markers}}
    </ul>
</div>
{{#js}}
require(['core/copy_to_clipboard']);
{{/js}}
